Show native views on the web: the app's DOM element under GPUI's canvas, its hole cut by the wgpu renderer (0047).

What:
- gpui_web: `NativeView::new` takes a `web_sys::HtmlElement`. GPUI moves it into a slot of its own, in a layer before
  the canvas (the canvas is raised above it, `position: relative; z-index: 1`, while views exist; the layer follows
  the canvas's fractional box wherever the page puts it): `<gpui-native-views>` holds a
  `<gpui-native-view-slot>` per view (`gpui::native_view_placement::visible`, `overflow: hidden`, coloured by
  `native_view_placement::background`) around a `<gpui-native-view>` (the view's bounds) around the element. Each
  frame, before the renderer draws, a view whose placement changed gets CSS `transform: translate(..)`, width and
  height: the bounds are whole device pixels already, so both boxes sit on the hole's pixels at any scale; unchanged
  views are not touched, so a frame that places nothing writes no style. A view not painted, or clipped away
  entirely, is `display: none` (an iframe keeps its page).
  Dropping the last handle removes the slot with the element in it; the last view takes the layer with it and gives
  the canvas its own styles back.
- gpui_wgpu: a WebGL2 canvas is premultiplied by its context's default whatever mode wgpu reports (only `Opaque`);
  0047's `native_view_support` says so (folded into 0047, Caveman C17).

New files `gpui_web/src/native_views.rs` (the DOM shell) and `native_view_layout.rs` (pure: `placement`; tested on
the host in patch-test.sh's web-pure crate). The slot lifecycle is ported from flutter/flutter
engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/platform_views/content_manager.dart (`renderContent`,
`_ensureContentCorrectlySized`, `clearPlatformView`), slots.dart (`createPlatformViewSlot`) and embedder.dart
(`_resetAnchor`, `disposeView`) @ 3.50.1 (BSD-3-Clause; third_party/flutter/PORTED.md lists what was dropped). As a
near-verbatim port it is exempt from the patch size limit (patch rule 4).

Pointer input over the views is 0068's, focus 0069's: until then the canvas takes every pointer event.

Tests: `native_view_layout::tests::placement_of_a_view`.

Why: `NativeView::new` failed on the web (xuckless/parallax#1). The window's canvas, its listeners and the frame are
private to gpui_web.

Upstream PR: not filed (filing paused, patch rule 14).

